sequenceDiagram
    participant FE as React Frontend
    participant API as FastAPI
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant ML as ML Model
    participant SOLR as Apache Solr

    Note over FE,SOLR: Startup Sequence (backend/main.py startup_pipeline)
    API->>DB: alembic upgrade head
    API->>ML: load best_model.pkl + scaler.pkl
    API->>DB: run_predictions_pipeline(limit=100)
    DB-->>API: machines/predictions/recs stored
    API->>SOLR: sync_data_to_solr()
    SOLR-->>API: indexed

    Note over FE,SOLR: Normal Request Flow
    FE->>API: GET /machines
    API->>DB: SELECT machines + latest prediction
    DB-->>API: machine rows
    API-->>FE: JSON array of MachineResponse

    FE->>API: GET /machines/{id}/risk
    API->>DB: get_machine_risk(machine_id)
    DB-->>API: risk data
    API-->>FE: risk JSON

    Note over FE,SOLR: Work Order Flow
    FE->>API: POST /work-orders {machine_id, priority, action}
    API->>DB: INSERT work_orders
    DB-->>API: work_order_id
    API-->>FE: {status: created, work_order_id}

    FE->>API: PATCH /work-orders/{id}/status {status: in_progress}
    API->>DB: UPDATE work_orders SET status
    DB-->>API: updated work order
    API-->>FE: {new_status: in_progress}

    FE->>API: PATCH /work-orders/{id}/status {status: completed}
    API->>DB: UPDATE SET status=completed, completed_at=now()
    DB-->>API: updated
    API-->>FE: {new_status: completed}

    Note over FE,SOLR: SQS Consumer Flow (background thread)
    loop Every 5 seconds
        API->>API: SQS.receive_message(sensor-events)
        API->>ML: predict_machine_failure(telemetry)
        ML-->>API: probability, failure_type
        API->>DB: upsert Machine + Prediction + Recommendation
    end
